    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "NYC type foundry founded 1989 by Jonathan Hoefler (briefly Hoefler & Frere-Jones with Tobias Frere-Jones, back to Hoefler&Co). Library includes Gotham, Archer, Sentinel, Whitney, Mercury, Knockout, Surveyor, Hoefler Text; clients have included Apple, NYT, Tiffany & Co, Obama For America. Acquired by Monotype in Sept 2021 (IP, typography.com, and the staff transferred, while founder Jonathan Hoefler and CEO Carleen Borsella stepped aside per reporting); typography.com continues operating as the Hoefler&Co brand within Monotype's Studio, per Monotype's own announcements. Org entry, Autonomy not applicable. Size (11 to 40) is the pre-migration baseline for the standalone foundry team and is unverified for the current Monotype-owned structure, flagged as an open question.",
      "source_url": "https://www.typography.com/about-us",
      "verified_at": "2026-07-27T00:17:56",
      "set_by": "agent"
    },
